  "worked_solution": "The function ${x}^{\u2032}(t)$ represents the rate at which the number of meters is changing at the moment $t$ seconds after starting its journey.\n\nTherefore, ${x}^{\u2032}(30)=10$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled increased at a rate of $10$ meters per second*",
